    Extracted VERBATIM 01.09.2026 from this device's OWN vendor partition image
    (/etc/vintf/manifest.xml, mounted read-only loop in VM, debugfs/mount) — not adapted from
    any other tree. This is the real, already-valid VINTF device manifest our stock
    vendor partition ships (built from many manifest_*.xml fragments by the stock build,
    listed in the original "Input:" comment preserved below). target-level="6" confirmed —
    A16 is served by level 6; raising it to 7 is an Android 17 question, not one for this build.
    vendor.skyroam.hardware.{file,socket} independently cross-confirmed live in our own DSU
    boot log (F3400: "HidlServiceManagement: Registered vendor.skyroam.hardware.socket@1.0
    ::ISocket/default").

    If the kernel line (<kernel target-level="8"/>) is ever bumped to 202404, the ROOT
    <manifest target-level="6"> can stay at 6: VINTF match rules allow kernel-level >= root-level,
    and all evidence for this build is for root level 6. Raising the root level is a separate,
    much heavier step (different vendor HAL/AIDL version requirements). This file reflects the
    device as it is.
-->
